Overlay patch 0057 (D24, port of Shipwright 0068 / D-087): MENU-PHASE SPLIT
for the spike probe (GS_MSLOW / GS_MENUWIN).

WHY. On Shipwright's phone, after the depth fix the remaining spikes sat in
0056's `menu` span (drawable acquired -> Gui::StartDraw returned), and this
split proved they were the UIKit run loop pumped from inside the ImGui frame:
LUS's invisible SDLAddRemoveDeviceEventHandler GuiWindow calls
SDL_PumpEvents() every frame, so all main-thread UIKit work (touches, the
touch overlay's full-screen repaint and CA commit, the 0.25 s poll) runs
inside Gui::DrawMenu. Ghostship's LUS has the same window; this ships the same
instrument so the phone log can show it (and the D26 overlay fix's effect).

WHAT IT MEASURES. Ten marks in the 2D frame (3D frames are skipped):
   P  Fast3dGui::ImGuiBackendNewFrame, before GfxRenderingAPIMetal::NewFrame
   A  ... after it        B  Gui::StartFrame, after ImGuiWMNewFrame (ImGui_ImplSDL2_NewFrame)
   C  Gui::DrawMenu entry (ImGui::NewFrame is B..C)
   D  before the menu bar  E  after the menu bar  F  after the port menu
   G  after the GuiWindows H  Fast3dGui::CalculateGameViewport entry  I  its exit
giving sub-buckets fb (A - drawable acquired), sdl, new, dock, bar, menu, win,
end, vp -- each with wall AND thread-CPU time -- plus every GuiWindow timed by
name.

OUTPUT (game thread, under 0056's gSohIos.SpikeProbe switch):
  GS_MSLOW    one line per frame whose menu phase took >= 4 ms wall (<= 20 / 10 s)
  GS_MENUWIN  one line per 10 s: frames, slow frames, wall/cpu avgs, each
              sub-bucket's avg all / slow / max, top-bucket counts, the four
              costliest GuiWindows (total ms / max).

Generate against a vendor tree with 0001..0056 applied and 0057 not applied.


